# Build output only. Everything a figure depends on stays in the tree.
#
# The rule this file is written against: the rust slice's published encode column had to
# be WITHDRAWN because a `.gitignore` rule (`[Bb]in/`, meant for .NET output) swallowed its
# measurement binaries, so the commit behind its log could not be rebuilt (its D19). R4's
# closing rule is that a figure whose harness is not in the tree cannot be defended. So the
# patterns here are anchored and specific, never a bare directory name that could match a
# source directory somewhere else, and `gen/audit_tracked.sh` checks from git's own answer
# rather than from reading this file.
/build/
# The shared core's build output for this slice. Three CARGO_TARGET_DIRs (timed,
# counting, rpc) under one directory, because R0 moved the crate itself to
# `ffi/poc/codec/crates/ak-core` and only the OUTPUT is this slice's.
/core-build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/build-odrbreak/
/build-o3/
